# Auth Architecture

## Session model
- Session is **in-memory only** — no localStorage, no cookies. Hard refresh clears session.
- `AuthProvider` in `client/context/AuthContext.tsx` owns all auth state.
- `App.tsx` wraps everything in `<AuthProvider>`. An `<AuthGate>` component inside conditionally renders `<SignIn>` (when `activeAccountId === null`) or the normal `<Routes>`.

## Accounts
Three pre-seeded accounts defined in `ACCOUNTS` constant in `AuthContext.tsx`:

| id | name | email | color |
|----|------|-------|-------|
| `alex` | Alex Chen | alex.chen@gmail.com | #0B57D0 |
| `priya` | Priya Patel | priya.patel@work.com | #33B679 |
| `sam` | Sam Kim | sam.kim@gmail.com | #8E24AA |

Account type lives in `client/types/auth.ts`:

interface Account { id, name, email, initials, color }
```

## AuthContext API (`useAuth()`)
```ts
activeAccountId: string | null   // null = signed out
activeAccount: Account | null
accounts: Account[]
events: CalendarEvent[]          // events for the active account only
addEvent(e): void
updateEvent(e): void
deleteEvent(id): void
signIn(accountId): void
switchAccount(accountId): void
signOut(): void
```

## Per-account event isolation
- `accountEvents: Record<string, CalendarEvent[]>` is stored in React state in `AuthProvider`.
- Each account gets its own seed events (see `generateAlexEvents`, `generatePriyaEvents`, `generateSamEvents` in `AuthContext.tsx`).
- `CalendarLayout` reads `events / addEvent / updateEvent / deleteEvent` from `useAuth()` instead of managing its own state. The `CalendarContext` shape is unchanged.
- Switching accounts instantly changes which event array is exposed via `useCalendar().events`.

## UI entry points
- **Sign-in screen**: `client/pages/SignIn.tsx` — centered card with 3 account rows; clicking calls `signIn()`.
- **Avatar + ProfileMenu**: Avatar button in `TopBar.tsx` (top-right). Opens `ProfileMenu.tsx`:
  - Section 1: current user (56px avatar, name, email, manage button)
  - Section 2: other accounts — click to switch
  - Section 3: Settings (opens TopBar settings panel) + Sign out
  - Dismiss: click outside (pointerdown listener), avatar button is excluded from outside-click check via `anchorRef`.
